# Controller + Model

## Controller (`app/controller/`)

Extend `Gemvc\Core\Controller`. Thin orchestration only.

```php
$model = $this->createModel(new UserModel()); // prefers APM/request wiring
$model = $this->request->mapPostToObject($model, [
    'email' => 'email',
    'name' => 'name',
    'password' => 'setPassword()', // calls setter on model
]);
if (!$model instanceof UserModel) {
    return $this->request->returnResponse();
}
return $model->createModel();
```

Lists: `return $this->createList($this->createModel(new UserModel()), 'id,email,role,created_at');`  
Pass an explicit column list so `protected` fields (e.g. password) stay out of payloads.

## Model (`app/model/`)

Usually `UserModel extends UserTable`. Put hashing, uniqueness, login, workflows here.

```php
public function createModel(): JsonResponse {
    $this->created_at = date('Y-m-d H:i:s');
    if (!$this->insertSingleQuery()) { // insertSingleQuery(): ?static — null on failure
        return Response::internalError('Failed: ' . $this->getError());
    }
    return Response::created($this, 1, 'User created successfully');
}
```

Use `Gemvc\Helper\CryptHelper` for passwords; `Gemvc\Http\JWTToken` for tokens. Prefer `Response::success|created|updated|deleted|notFound|unauthorized|forbidden|internalError`.

### Composition models

Non-Table models (e.g. auth orchestration) may call other Models/Tables for multi-step workflows. Still return `JsonResponse` from the API-facing methods. Prefer going through a Model for domain reads (e.g. access map) instead of ad-hoc `QueryBuilder` in the composition class when a Table already exists.

### Read-only view models

For `ViewTable` subclasses: Model usually extends the view Table. Implement `read` / `list` / select helpers only.

- Framework already blocks row insert/update/delete on `ViewTable` — do not call them from the Model.
- If you still expose `createModel` / `updateModel` / `deleteModel`, return `Response::forbidden(...)` (or omit those methods from the API).
- Nesting (e.g. user + payments list): load flat view rows and/or base Tables, then shape JSON in the Model — views stay flat.
